We investigate the impact of recent $b 	o c$ anomalies on the $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$ decay within the $U_1$ leptoquark framework. By analyzing the leptoquark contributions to the $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$ form factors, we find that the $U_1$ leptoquark can significantly enhance the branching ratio of this decay, potentially exceeding the $10^{-2}$ threshold. Furthermore, we find that the leptoquark's influence on the $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$ decay is highly sensitive to the Wilson coefficients of the $b 	o c$ operators, which are constrained by recent $b 	o c$ anomalies. Specifically, we find that the leptoquark's contribution to the branching ratio of $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$ is highly suppressed when the Wilson coefficients of the $b 	o c$ operators are consistent with the SM expectations, but can be significantly enhanced when these coefficients are large, as indicated by recent $b 	o c$ anomalies.
